tings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Carolina remains one of the closest presidential battlegrounds, with a partisan lean of about one point Republican. The 2028 race is fully open: the incumbent president is term-limited, and neither party has settled on a nominee. Early 2028 primary coverage suggests Republicans are coalescing around a successor field while Democrats are still sorting out their own contest, but none of this yet translates into a measurable general-election edge in the state.\n\nNo general-election polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are available for this race, so the forecast leans on structural fundamentals alone. Those fundamentals describe a near-even state with a slight Republican tilt, wide uncertainty, and genuine two-party competitiveness heading into the campaign.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4508, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4639, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4659, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4636, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4637, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4628, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4642, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}]}